Package: SBayesEigen
Type: Package
Title: Fast SBayes-Style Polygenic Risk Scores from Eigen-Decomposed LD
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yihe", "Yang", email = "yxy1234@case.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6563-3579")),
    person("Christopher", "Chang", role = c("ctb", "cph"), comment = "bundled pgenlib"))
Description: Builds polygenic risk scores from GWAS summary statistics and
    eigen-decomposed LD blocks in the SBayesRC layout (blockN.eigen.bin). The
    LD reference is built directly from PLINK BED or PGEN genotypes with a
    bit-plane correlation kernel and a partial eigendecomposition that forms
    only the leading eigenvectors. Summary data are tidied and imputed in the
    eigen space. The marginal effects are rotated into each block's eigenbasis,
    where the likelihood is diagonal, and the effects receive a six-class
    mixture prior (an exact zero plus variance ratios 1:10:100:1000:10000)
    fitted by variational EM with SQUAREM acceleration. A built-in LD score
    regression gives the heritability start value and a heavy-tailed prior on
    the genetic variance. The core is C++ with OpenMP.
